WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:00.876
Hello!

00:00:00.876 --> 00:00:01.668
Hi!

00:00:02.419 --> 00:00:05.797
Reese Witherspoon:
When we got together, a long
time ago, we were talking about how country music

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:08.759
should stop limiting people and
start opening doors.

00:00:08.759 --> 00:00:11.011
Kacey Musgraves:
It’s music brought over from all
over the world. 

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.721
The bluegrass, the folk, the
gospel.

00:00:12.721 --> 00:00:15.140
Kacey Musgraves:
There’s so many threads woven
through country music.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.851
♪♪

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.853
Reese Witherspoon:
This is “My Kind Of Country”

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:24.274
Reese Witherspoon:
A music competition that travels
the globe to break the next country music star.

00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:27.027
♪♪

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:30.030
Reese Witherspoon:
We’re partnering with three
trail-blazing, country musicians,

00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:34.034
Jimmie Allen:
It took me eleven years to get a record deal.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.160
I lived in my car.

00:00:36.411 --> 00:00:39.206
Mickey Guyton:
I was the first black female
solo artist

00:00:39.206 --> 00:00:42.793
Mickey Guyton:
to earn a Grammy Nomination in a
Country category.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:46.171
Orville Peck:
My mask allows me to be more
vulnerable

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:48.799
and share my perspective as a
gay country artist.

00:00:49.216 --> 00:00:53.095
Reese Witherspoon:
They are gonna search the world
for musicians and invite them to Nashville.

00:00:53.345 --> 00:00:54.221
Oh my gosh!

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:59.601
Ultimately, there will be one
person who wins a life-changing
prize from Apple Music.

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:00.519
♪♪

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:03.272
This is the reason why you let
your kids follow their dreams.

00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:05.899
♪♪

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.568
Got my bag packed here!
Nashville, I’m coming.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:12.948
♪♪

00:01:12.948 --> 00:01:14.658
Welcome to Nashville!

00:01:14.658 --> 00:01:15.617
♪♪

00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:17.828
Mickey Guyton:
They say country music is three
chords and the truth.

00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:20.247
It’s singing about life and your
life story.

00:01:20.247 --> 00:01:23.542
♪♪

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:28.422
I don’t feel like I can express
myself in English so I sing it
in Spanish.

00:01:28.422 --> 00:01:32.134
♪♪

00:01:32.134 --> 00:01:37.347
I struggle with my own inner
voice a little bit but when I
get to sing I feel totally whole.

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:37.764
(Cheering)

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:42.728
That was so sincere and
beautiful and that is country
music.

00:01:42.728 --> 00:01:45.105
♪♪

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:49.484
There’s just so much potential
for something I don’t think
anybody’s ever seen before in country music.

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:51.111
♪♪

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.655
The people that I love in
country music, they don’t look
like me.

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:55.282
Camille:
I’m ready to show people
what they’ve been missing.

00:01:55.282 --> 00:02:00.954
♪♪

